Here's how to implement all three:

### 1. Custom "Cancel" back button on `EditProductPage.xaml`

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.Views.EditProductPage">

    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior TextOverride="Cancel"
                            Command="{Binding CancelCommand}" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>

    <!-- your form content -->
</ContentPage>
```

### 2. ViewModel with cancel logic and unsaved-changes flag

```csharp
public partial class EditProductViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    [ObservableProperty]
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task Cancel()
    {
        if (HasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool discard = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard them?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!discard) return;
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }
}
```

### 3. Navigation guard in `AppShell.xaml.cs`

This catches the **hardware/gesture back** (swipe, system back button) which bypasses `BackButtonBehavior.Command`:

```csharp
public partial class AppShell : Shell
{
    protected override async void OnNavigating(ShellNavigatingEventArgs args)
    {
        base.OnNavigating(args);

        if (args.Source == ShellNavigationSource.Pop
            && CurrentPage is EditProductPage page
            && page.BindingContext is EditProductViewModel vm
            && vm.HasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            var deferral = args.GetDeferral();

            bool discard = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard them?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!discard)
                args.Cancel();

            deferral.Complete();
        }
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `BackButtonBehavior` replaces the back arrow with "Cancel" and routes taps through your command.
- `OnNavigating` with `GetDeferral()` intercepts system-back/swipe gestures — the deferral is **required** for async checks like `DisplayAlert`.
- Check `args.Source == ShellNavigationSource.Pop` so you only guard backward navigation, not forward pushes.
